    "media:imagetext": "The Proud Bird\nCONTINENTAL AIRLINES\nTHE CONTINENTAL AIRLINES McDONNELL DOUG-\nLAS DC-10 (Series 10.) Fuel capacity: 145,201 Ibs. Or\n21,671 gallons, or enough to run an automobile 329,085\nmiles — more than 13 trips around the world! Cruising\nspeed: Mach 0.82. 544 mph. Range: 3,300 miles. Wing\nspan length: 155 ft., 4 inches. Aircraft length: 181 ft., 3\ninches. Horizontal stabilizer: 71 ft., 2 inches (which is\ngreater than the length of a DC-3 which measures only\n54 feet, 6½ inches.) Vertical stabilizer: 58 ft., 1 inch.\nPowered by: 3 General Electric CF6-6D engines with a\ntotal take-off thrust of 120,000 Ibs.\nA John D. Clayton photograph\nPLACE\nSTAMP\nHERE\n2015.166.0577",
